Phantom Mirage I
================

Phantom Mirage I is part of the Phantom deception product range.

Phantom Mirage I is based on Honeyd
-----------------------------------

Phantom Mirage I is a renamed and modified version of Honeyd, the virtual
honeypot daemon written by Niels Provos <provos@citi.umich.edu>
(Copyright (c) 2002-2007 Niels Provos), with later contributions by
DataSoft Corp (Nova), the Debian packagers (Javier Fernandez-Sanguino Pena
and others) and the other authors credited in the source files, the
ChangeLog and debian/copyright.

Honeyd is free software released under the GNU General Public License,
version 2 or (at your option) any later version. Phantom Mirage I is
distributed under the same terms; the full licence text is in LICENSE.
All original copyright notices, licence notices and credits in the source
files are retained unchanged. Some files carry additional or different
permissive notices (e.g. BSD-style); those also remain in force.

The rename (2026, Daniel de Jager <ddejager@dandejager.com>) changed
program, package, path and environment-variable names only; it does not
change the licence or the authorship of the original code. "Honeyd" is the
name of the original project; Phantom Mirage I is not endorsed by its
authors.

Rename map
----------

  honeyd                      -> phantom-mirage
  honeydctl                   -> phantom-mirage-ctl
  honeydstats                 -> phantom-mirage-stats
  hsniff                      -> phantom-mirage-sniff
  libhoneyd.so                -> libphantom-mirage.so
  /usr/share/honeyd           -> /usr/share/phantom-mirage
  /usr/lib/honeyd             -> /usr/lib/phantom-mirage
  /etc/honeypot               -> /etc/phantom-mirage
  /etc/honeypot/honeyd.conf   -> /etc/phantom-mirage/phantom-mirage.conf
  /var/log/honeypot           -> /var/log/phantom-mirage
  /var/run/honeyd/honeyd.sock -> /run/phantom-mirage/phantom-mirage.sock
  /var/run/honeyd.pid         -> /run/phantom-mirage.pid
  ~/.config/honeyd            -> ~/.config/phantom-mirage
  HONEYD_* environment        -> PHANTOM_MIRAGE_* (HONEYD_* still accepted,
                                 deprecated, and still exported to scripts)
  Debian honeyd/honeyd-common -> phantom-mirage/phantom-mirage-common
  honeyd.service              -> phantom-mirage.service

Kept for compatibility: the embedded Python module is still "honeyd" and
the Python service hooks are still honeyd_init/honeyd_readdata/
honeyd_writedata/honeyd_end; plugin headers still install under
<includedir>/honeyd so existing #include <honeyd/...> lines keep working.
